@lang en
IMPORT `pti-tests-fixtures`

-- TESTS for Part 5 (claims procedure): the day of last treatment, the three time limits
-- and the forfeiture, PTI's time to pay, the documents, their form, and direct billing.
-- Dates are worked by hand: from 3 March 2026, 30 days is 2 April and 180 days is 30 August;
-- from 1 May 2026, 120 days is 29 August. A failing assertion is a finding.

§ `Tests — Part 5`

§§ `Helpers`

GIVEN e IS A `The event`
      lines IS A LIST OF `A claim item`
      f IS A `The filing of the claim`
GIVETH A `The claim`
`a claim for` e `with the lines` lines `, filed as` f MEANS
    `The claim` WITH
        `the insured person`                    IS `the insured person`
        `the policy`                            IS `the standard policy`
        `the event`                             IS e
        `the items`                             IS lines
        `the filing`                            IS f
        `other insurance`                       IS NOTHING
        `already counted earlier in the period` IS EMPTY

GIVEN notified IS A MAYBE DATE
      filed IS A MAYBE DATE
      asked IS A MAYBE DATE
      further IS A MAYBE DATE
      fm IS A BOOLEAN
      docs IS A LIST OF `A submitted document`
GIVETH A `The filing of the claim`
`a filing: notified` notified `, filed` filed `, more asked for` asked `, more given` further `, force majeure` fm `, documents` docs MEANS
    `The filing of the claim` WITH
        `the date PTI was notified`                     IS notified
        `the date the claim file was submitted`         IS filed
        `the date PTI asked for more documents`         IS asked
        `the date the further documents were submitted` IS further
        `prevented by force majeure`                    IS fm
        `the documents submitted`                       IS docs
        `an invoice gives only a combined total`        IS FALSE

GIVEN filed IS A DATE
GIVETH A `The claim`
`the standard stay claim, filed on` filed MEANS
    `a claim for` `the standard illness event` `with the lines` (LIST `a clean benefit 1 line`) `, filed as` (`a filing: notified` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 10)) `, filed` (JUST filed) `, more asked for` NOTHING `, more given` NOTHING `, force majeure` FALSE `, documents` EMPTY)

GIVEN d IS A `A claim document`
      f IS A `A form of document`
GIVETH A `A submitted document`
`a document:` d `, as` f MEANS
    `A submitted document` WITH
        `the document`                                                         IS d
        `the form`                                                             IS f
        `bears the round stamp of the medical establishment`                   IS TRUE
        `shows the establishment's tax code and business registration number`  IS FALSE

GIVEN it IS A `A claim item`
      e IS A `The event`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A claim document`
`the documents for the line` it `for the event` e MEANS
    `the documents Part 5 asks for, for` (`the line` it `in` (`a claim by` `the insured person` `under` `the standard policy` `for` e `with the lines` (LIST it)))

GIVEN k IS A `A kind of accident`
      serious IS A BOOLEAN
      third IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The event`
`an accident event of the kind` k `, serious:` serious `, third party:` third MEANS
    `an event: cause` `an accident` `, accident` (JUST (`The accident` WITH `the date` IS YMD 2026 3 1, `where it happened` IS `Vietnam`, `sudden` IS TRUE, `caused by an external and visible force on the body` IS TRUE, `outside the insured person's will and control` IS TRUE, `the direct cause of the death or the injury` IS TRUE, `the injury was the first consequence of the accident` IS TRUE, `the injury was an accumulation of accidents or injuries` IS FALSE, `the injury was caused, directly or indirectly, by the aggravation of a weakness, defect, degeneration or illness that existed before cover began` IS FALSE, `the injury was caused solely by the accident, not by illness, declining health or nerves, time or age` IS TRUE, `the kind` IS k, `serious` IS serious, `a third party was involved` IS third)) `, illness` NOTHING `, diagnoses` EMPTY `, circumstances` EMPTY `, stay` (JUST `the standard stay`)

`a death from an accident in daily life` MEANS
    `The event` WITH
        `the cause`                                IS `an accident`
        `the accident`                             IS JUST `the standard accident`
        `the illness`                              IS NOTHING
        `the conditions diagnosed`                 IS EMPTY
        `the circumstances`                        IS EMPTY
        `the sporting activity`                    IS NOTHING
        `the hospital stay`                        IS NOTHING
        `the date of death`                        IS JUST (YMD 2026 3 2)
        `the cause of death unknown`               IS FALSE
        `the disablement`                          IS NOTHING
        `the date the surgery was first ordered`   IS NOTHING
        `the date of the outpatient diagnosis`     IS NOTHING

`an outpatient illness event` MEANS
    `The event` WITH
        `the cause`                                IS `an illness`
        `the accident`                             IS NOTHING
        `the illness`                              IS JUST `the standard illness`
        `the conditions diagnosed`                 IS LIST `a condition the Rules do not name`
        `the circumstances`                        IS EMPTY
        `the sporting activity`                    IS NOTHING
        `the hospital stay`                        IS NOTHING
        `the date of death`                        IS NOTHING
        `the cause of death unknown`               IS FALSE
        `the disablement`                          IS NOTHING
        `the date the surgery was first ordered`   IS NOTHING
        `the date of the outpatient diagnosis`     IS JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)

§§ `Clause 1 — the day of last treatment and the time limits`
#ASSERT `the day of last treatment for` (`the standard stay claim, filed on` (YMD 2026 3 20)) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 3
#ASSERT `the day of last treatment for` (`a claim for` `an outpatient illness event` `with the lines` EMPTY `, filed as` `a filing in time`) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 1
-- A death with no treatment: the clause fixes no day of last treatment.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day of last treatment for` (`a claim for` `a death from an accident in daily life` `with the lines` EMPTY `, filed as` `a filing in time`) BECAUSE "Part 5 clause 1 fixes the day of last treatment only for a hospital stay and for outpatient treatment"
#ASSERT `the last day to notify PTI of` (`the standard stay claim, filed on` (YMD 2026 3 20)) EQUALS YMD 2026 4 2
#ASSERT `the last day to submit the claim file for` (`the standard stay claim, filed on` (YMD 2026 3 20)) EQUALS YMD 2026 8 30
#ASSERT `the last day to submit further documents asked for on` (YMD 2026 5 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 8 29
-- Filed on the 180th day: not late; on the 181st: refused in full; with force majeure: not.
#ASSERT NOT (`clause 1 refuses in full, for lateness,` (`the standard stay claim, filed on` (YMD 2026 8 30)))
#ASSERT `clause 1 refuses in full, for lateness,` (`the standard stay claim, filed on` (YMD 2026 8 31))
#ASSERT NOT (`clause 1 refuses in full, for lateness,` (`a claim for` `the standard illness event` `with the lines` (LIST `a clean benefit 1 line`) `, filed as` (`a filing: notified` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 10)) `, filed` (JUST (YMD 2026 8 31)) `, more asked for` NOTHING `, more given` NOTHING `, force majeure` TRUE `, documents` EMPTY)))
-- Further documents asked for on 1 May: given on 29 August, in time; on 30 August, late.
#ASSERT NOT (`clause 1 refuses in full, for lateness,` (`a claim for` `the standard illness event` `with the lines` (LIST `a clean benefit 1 line`) `, filed as` (`a filing: notified` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 10)) `, filed` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 20)) `, more asked for` (JUST (YMD 2026 5 1)) `, more given` (JUST (YMD 2026 8 29)) `, force majeure` FALSE `, documents` EMPTY)))
#ASSERT `clause 1 refuses in full, for lateness,` (`a claim for` `the standard illness event` `with the lines` (LIST `a clean benefit 1 line`) `, filed as` (`a filing: notified` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 10)) `, filed` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 20)) `, more asked for` (JUST (YMD 2026 5 1)) `, more given` (JUST (YMD 2026 8 30)) `, force majeure` FALSE `, documents` EMPTY))
-- Not filed at all: the question cannot be answered yet.
#ASSERT REFUSED `clause 1 refuses in full, for lateness,` (`a claim for` `the standard illness event` `with the lines` (LIST `a clean benefit 1 line`) `, filed as` (`a filing: notified` NOTHING `, filed` NOTHING `, more asked for` NOTHING `, more given` NOTHING `, force majeure` FALSE `, documents` EMPTY)) BECAUSE "the claim file has not been submitted"
-- Notice on 3 April, the 31st day, is late; the claim is still not refused (fork F40).
#ASSERT `the notice was late, for` (`a claim for` `the standard illness event` `with the lines` (LIST `a clean benefit 1 line`) `, filed as` (`a filing: notified` (JUST (YMD 2026 4 3)) `, filed` (JUST (YMD 2026 4 10)) `, more asked for` NOTHING `, more given` NOTHING `, force majeure` FALSE `, documents` EMPTY))
#ASSERT NOT (`the notice was late, for` (`a claim for` `the standard illness event` `with the lines` (LIST `a clean benefit 1 line`) `, filed as` (`a filing: notified` (JUST (YMD 2026 4 2)) `, filed` (JUST (YMD 2026 4 10)) `, more asked for` NOTHING `, more given` NOTHING `, force majeure` FALSE `, documents` EMPTY)))
#ASSERT NOT (`clause 1 refuses in full, for lateness,` (`a claim for` `the standard illness event` `with the lines` (LIST `a clean benefit 1 line`) `, filed as` (`a filing: notified` (JUST (YMD 2026 4 3)) `, filed` (JUST (YMD 2026 4 10)) `, more asked for` NOTHING `, more given` NOTHING `, force majeure` FALSE `, documents` EMPTY)))
-- PTI's own time to pay: the Rules state none.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day for PTI to pay` (`the standard stay claim, filed on` (YMD 2026 3 20)) BECAUSE "Part 5 states no time within which PTI must assess or pay a claim"

-- The duties as traces. Notice on day 30: fulfilled; nothing by day 31: breached.
#TRACE `Part 5 clause 1: the insured person or the heir must notify PTI` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the insured person or the heir` DOES `notify PTI of the claim` AT 30
#TRACE `Part 5 clause 1: the insured person or the heir must notify PTI` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 31)
#TRACE `Part 5 clause 1: the insured person or the heir must submit the claim file` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the insured person or the heir` DOES `submit the claim file` AT 180
#TRACE `Part 5 clause 1: the insured person or the heir must submit the further documents` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 121)

§§ `The form of documents`
#ASSERT `the kind of` `the pharmacy invoice` EQUALS `a financial document`
#ASSERT `the kind of` `the discharge paper` EQUALS `a medical document`
#ASSERT `the kind of` `the death certificate` EQUALS `another document`
#ASSERT (`a document:` `the pharmacy invoice` `, as` `an original`) `is in an acceptable form`
#ASSERT NOT ((`a document:` `the pharmacy invoice` `, as` `a copy certified as a true copy by a competent authority`) `is in an acceptable form`)
#ASSERT (`a document:` `the discharge paper` `, as` `a copy certified as a true copy by a competent authority`) `is in an acceptable form`
#ASSERT NOT ((`a document:` `the discharge paper` `, as` `a plain copy`) `is in an acceptable form`)
#ASSERT (`a document:` `a copy of both sides of the driving licence and the vehicle registration` `, as` `a plain copy`) `is in an acceptable form`
-- The medical record book: no round stamp but the tax code and registration number, yes;
-- neither, no.
#ASSERT (`A submitted document` WITH `the document` IS `the medical record book or examination slip`, `the form` IS `an original`, `bears the round stamp of the medical establishment` IS FALSE, `shows the establishment's tax code and business registration number` IS TRUE) `is in an acceptable form`
#ASSERT NOT ((`A submitted document` WITH `the document` IS `the medical record book or examination slip`, `the form` IS `an original`, `bears the round stamp of the medical establishment` IS FALSE, `shows the establishment's tax code and business registration number` IS FALSE) `is in an acceptable form`)

§§ `Clause 2 — the documents each claim needs`
-- Programme I medical expenses after an accident in daily life.
#ASSERT `the documents for the line` (`a line under` `Programme I: medical expenses for an accidental injury` `for` `surgery` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `of` 2_000_000) `for the event` `the standard accident event` EQUALS LIST `an accident report by the insured person or the beneficiary`, `the medical record book or examination slip`, `receipts or invoices for imaging, tests and ultrasound, itemised by kind of cost`
-- ... at work.
#ASSERT `the documents for the line` (`a line under` `Programme I: medical expenses for an accidental injury` `for` `surgery` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `of` 2_000_000) `for the event` (`an accident event of the kind` `an accident at work` `, serious:` FALSE `, third party:` FALSE) EQUALS LIST `an accident report certified by the employer`, `the medical record book or examination slip`, `receipts or invoices for imaging, tests and ultrasound, itemised by kind of cost`
-- ... on the road, nobody else involved: the licence copy, not the police record.
#ASSERT `the documents for the line` (`a line under` `Programme I: medical expenses for an accidental injury` `for` `surgery` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `of` 2_000_000) `for the event` (`an accident event of the kind` `a traffic accident` `, serious:` FALSE `, third party:` FALSE) EQUALS LIST `a copy of both sides of the driving licence and the vehicle registration`, `the medical record book or examination slip`, `receipts or invoices for imaging, tests and ultrasound, itemised by kind of cost`
-- ... on the road, with a third party: the police record too.
#ASSERT `the documents for the line` (`a line under` `Programme I: medical expenses for an accidental injury` `for` `surgery` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `of` 2_000_000) `for the event` (`an accident event of the kind` `a traffic accident` `, serious:` FALSE `, third party:` TRUE) EQUALS LIST `an accident record certified by the police or the local authority`, `a copy of both sides of the driving licence and the vehicle registration`, `the medical record book or examination slip`, `receipts or invoices for imaging, tests and ultrasound, itemised by kind of cost`
-- Medicine: the prescription and the pharmacy invoice as well.
#ASSERT `the documents for the line` (`a line under` `Programme I: medical expenses for an accidental injury` `for` `medicines` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `of` 2_000_000) `for the event` `the standard accident event` EQUALS LIST `an accident report by the insured person or the beneficiary`, `the medical record book or examination slip`, `receipts or invoices for imaging, tests and ultrasound, itemised by kind of cost`, `the prescription`, `the pharmacy invoice`
-- Death: the death certificate and the certificate of the right to inherit.
#ASSERT `the documents for the line` (`a fixed-sum line under` `Programme I: death from an accident` `on` (YMD 2026 3 2)) `for the event` `a death from an accident in daily life` EQUALS LIST `an accident report by the insured person or the beneficiary`, `the death certificate`, `the certificate of the right to inherit`
-- Programme II, outside the network: benefit 1; benefit 2 adds the certificate of surgery.
#ASSERT `the documents for the line` `a clean benefit 1 line` `for the event` `the standard illness event` EQUALS LIST `the discharge paper`, `invoices for the costs of treatment during the hospital stay`
#ASSERT `the documents for the line` (`a line under` `Programme II benefit 2: surgery for illness` `for` `the surgeon` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `of` 10_000_000) `for the event` `the standard illness event` EQUALS LIST `the discharge paper`, `invoices for the costs of treatment during the hospital stay`, `the certificate of surgery`
-- In the network: nothing asked of the insured person.
#ASSERT `the documents for the line` `a clean benefit 1 line` `for the event` (`an illness, with the stay` (`a stay from` (YMD 2026 3 1) `to` (YMD 2026 3 3) `, hours` 50 `, admitted` TRUE `, overnight` TRUE `, at` `a network hospital in Vietnam`)) EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `the documents for the line` (`an outside line under` `Programme II other benefit: costs before admission` `for` `examination` `on` (YMD 2026 2 20) `of` 500_000 `at` `a hospital in Vietnam` `, ordered by` (JUST `a licensed doctor`)) `for the event` `the standard illness event` EQUALS LIST `orders and results of tests, ultrasound or X-ray before admission`, `invoices for imaging and tests before admission, with an itemised statement`
#ASSERT `the documents for the line` (`a line under` `Programme II other benefit: transport` `for` `an ambulance of a hospital, of a lawful clinic, or of the 115 service` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `of` 1_000_000) `for the event` `the standard illness event` EQUALS LIST `financial receipts or invoices in the form the Ministry of Finance issues`, `records of treatment in the emergency room`
-- A taxi: no document is listed.
#ASSERT `the documents for the line` (`a line under` `Programme II other benefit: transport` `for` `a taxi` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `of` 300_000) `for the event` `the standard illness event` EQUALS EMPTY
-- The optional benefits' own lists.
#ASSERT `the documents for the line` (`a line under` `benefit 3: dental treatment` `for` `scaling` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `of` 300_000) `for the event` `an outpatient illness event` EQUALS LIST `medical documents, such as the dental treatment slip or X-ray films`, `financial receipts or invoices in the form the Ministry of Finance issues`, `invoices or receipts giving details of the teeth treated and the method`
#ASSERT `the documents for the line` (`a fixed-sum line under` `optional benefit 5: income allowance` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1)) `for the event` `the standard accident event` EQUALS LIST `an accident record`, `the medical record book or examination slip`, `the discharge paper`
#ASSERT `the documents for the line` (`a line under` `benefit 4: maternity care` `for` `a caesarean section` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `of` 30_000_000) `for the event` `the standard illness event` EQUALS LIST `the discharge paper`, `invoices for the costs of treatment during the hospital stay`, `the certificate of surgery`
#ASSERT `the documents for the line` (`an outside line under` `optional benefit 2: outpatient treatment` `for` `medicines prescribed by a doctor` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `of` 300_000 `at` `a hospital in Vietnam` `, ordered by` (JUST `a licensed doctor`)) `for the event` `an outpatient illness event` EQUALS LIST `the medical record book or examination slip`, `the prescription`, `the pharmacy invoice`
-- Benefit 6, for a disablement: the death certificate is on the list (finding X17).
#ASSERT `the documents for the line` (`a fixed-sum line under` `benefit 6: total permanent disablement from illness` `on` (YMD 2026 3 5)) `for the event` `the standard illness event` EQUALS LIST `the death certificate`, `the relevant medical documents`, `the certificate of the right to inherit`

§§ `A complete claim file`
#ASSERT `the claim file is complete, for` (`a claim for` `the standard illness event` `with the lines` (LIST `a clean benefit 1 line`) `, filed as` (`a filing: notified` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 10)) `, filed` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 20)) `, more asked for` NOTHING `, more given` NOTHING `, force majeure` FALSE `, documents` (LIST (`a document:` `the discharge paper` `, as` `a copy certified as a true copy by a competent authority`), (`a document:` `invoices for the costs of treatment during the hospital stay` `, as` `an original`))))
-- The invoices as a certified copy: missing.
#ASSERT `the documents missing from` (`a claim for` `the standard illness event` `with the lines` (LIST `a clean benefit 1 line`) `, filed as` (`a filing: notified` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 10)) `, filed` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 20)) `, more asked for` NOTHING `, more given` NOTHING `, force majeure` FALSE `, documents` (LIST (`a document:` `the discharge paper` `, as` `an original`), (`a document:` `invoices for the costs of treatment during the hospital stay` `, as` `a copy certified as a true copy by a competent authority`)))) EQUALS LIST `invoices for the costs of treatment during the hospital stay`
#ASSERT `the documents missing from` (`the standard stay claim, filed on` (YMD 2026 3 20)) EQUALS LIST `the discharge paper`, `invoices for the costs of treatment during the hospital stay`

§§ `Direct billing and payment`
#ASSERT `the part of a bill of` 5_000_000 `the insured person pays, PTI paying` 3_000_000 EQUALS 2_000_000
#ASSERT `the part of a bill of` 5_000_000 `the insured person pays, PTI paying` 5_000_000 EQUALS 0
-- A copy of the birth certificate for a child under 14: at 13 yes, at 14 no.
#ASSERT `a copy of the birth certificate is shown for` (`a person born on` (YMD 2012 6 1)) `on` (YMD 2026 3 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`a copy of the birth certificate is shown for` (`a person born on` (YMD 2012 1 1)) `on` (YMD 2026 3 1))
-- Part 2 A: the legal representative; who may be paid.
#ASSERT `Part 2 A: the legal representative may act for the insured person, who has lost capacity or died:` TRUE
#ASSERT `Part 2 A: PTI may pay the benefit to` `a lawful heir of the insured person` `, direct billing being in issue:` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Part 2 A: PTI may pay the benefit to` `a provider of medical treatment, care or services to the insured person` `, direct billing being in issue:` FALSE)
#ASSERT `Part 2 A: PTI may pay the benefit to` `a provider of medical treatment, care or services to the insured person` `, direct billing being in issue:` TRUE
-- The insured person's duties under direct billing: admitted on day 0, discharged on day 3.
#TRACE `direct billing: the insured person's duties, admitted on day` 0 `and discharged on day` 3 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the insured person or the heir` DOES `present the insurance card and an identity card or passport` AT 0
    PARTY `the insured person or the heir` DOES `sign the treatment documents` AT 3
    PARTY `the insured person or the heir` DOES `pay the costs beyond the cover before leaving the hospital` AT 3
#TRACE `direct billing: the insured person's duties, admitted on day` 0 `and discharged on day` 3 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the insured person or the heir` DOES `present the insurance card and an identity card or passport` AT 0
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4)
